AienOS release keys

alpha release key (Ed25519), in use from alpha-20261026.1
  raw public key (hex):  ff949504b427680039d53c33c85c448546b57d590eb1ecee3bb2ed6c2eaaf54a
  PEM (SubjectPublicKeyInfo), also keys/release.pub.pem:
    -----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
    MCowBQYDK2VwAyEA/5SVBLQnaAA51TwzyFxEhUa1fVkOsezuO7LtbC6q9Uo=
    -----END PUBLIC KEY-----

  Status: an ALPHA key. Created 2026-10-26 on the build machine; the private seed lives
  only in a TPM-bound vault there and was never written to disk in clear. Drake Stapleton
  approved it as the alpha trust root on 2026-10-26. It is not a ceremony key: before
  beta it is replaced by a key made at a witnessed offline ceremony, and that change is
  announced here and on https://www.aienos.com/alpha/.

What it signs: the bytes of each release's SHA256SUMS (Ed25519 over the raw file, no
prehash). SHA256SUMS lists the bundle, install.sh, aienos.om and these key files.

Check a release with stock tools (OpenSSL 3.0 or newer):
  openssl pkeyutl -verify -pubin -inkey release.pub.pem -rawin \
      -in SHA256SUMS -sigfile SHA256SUMS.sig
  sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
